#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:1
msgid "pyemscripten_2026_5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:3
msgid ""
"By default, all builds of the Pyodide runtime with Python 3.15 use the "
"`pyemscripten_2026_5` platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:6
msgid ""
"This section reflects the planned definition for the `pyemscripten_2026_5` "
"platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:9
msgid "Platform Specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:11
msgid "CPython and Emscripten Version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:13
msgid "**CPython**: 3.15"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:14
msgid "**Emscripten**: 6.0.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:16
msgid "Unwinding ABIs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:18
msgid ""
"C++ libraries are built with WebAssembly exception handling (`-fwasm-"
"exceptions`) and WebAssembly-based `setjmp`/`longjmp` (`-"
"sSUPPORT_LONGJMP=wasm`). To enable exceptions and `setjmp`/`longjmp`, `-"
"fwasm-exceptions` must be passed at compile time and link time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:23
msgid "Rust Toolchain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:25
msgid ""
"When building Rust packages to target the `pyemscripten_2026_5` platform, "
"use Rust version 1.93.0 or later. As of writing this, we default to Rust "
"1.97.1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:28
msgid "Runtime Library Loading Path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:30
msgid ""
"There is full support for `RPATH`. The dynamic loader will only load "
"dependencies that are properly specified on the `RPATH`, just being in `/lib/"
"python3.15/site-packages/wheel_name.libs` is not sufficient."
msgstr ""

