#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:57
msgid "Changes from pyemscripten_2026_0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:59
msgid ""
"The only change from `pyemscripten_2026_0` to `pyemscripten_2026_5` is that "
"Emscripten was upgraded from **5.0.3** to **6.0.5**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:62
msgid "Migration Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:64
msgid ""
"There are three changes in Emscripten 6.0.5 that may cause trouble building "
"Python packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:66
msgid "`-shared` links a real dynamic library instead of a static library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:68
msgid ""
"Until Emscripten 6.0.0, the `-shared` flag was not really respected, and "
"passing it would generate a `.so` file that was actually a static archive. "
"This difference in behavior can lead to differences in linking behavior. "
"Generally this shows up when running `configure`. Pass `-sFAKE_DYLIBS` as an "
"ldflag to opt into the old behavior of ignoring `-shared`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:73
msgid "OpenMP Supported by Emscripten 6.0.5 but not by Pyodide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:75
msgid ""
"OpenMP is supported by Emscripten 6.0.5 but it requires pthreads. (On the "
"other hand, `-fopenmp-simd` works fine.) Pyodide's compiler and linker "
"wrapper will exit with a nonzero status code if `-fopenmp` or related flags "
"are passed, but if emcc is invoked directly it will successfully link a "
"shared library that can only be loaded by a pthreads-enabled binary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:81
msgid "Bug involving C++ exceptions in optimizing builds with dwarf symbols"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:83
msgid ""
"A program with C++ exceptions and dwarf symbols may crash in wasm-opt with a "
"message like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:84
msgid ""
"wasm-opt: wasm-debug.cpp:439: void wasm::Debug::AddrExprMap::add(Expression "
"*, const BinaryLocations::Span): Assertion `!endMap.contains(span.end)' "
"failed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:87
msgid "To work around this, disable dwarf."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/abi/315.md:89
msgid "https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten/issues/27449"
msgstr ""
